{"results":[{"id":"6af1c04bc9cb5773cc15b8bc","name":"The Industry Leader in Enterprise Brand Protection","description":"A sophisticated phishing campaign has been identified targeting hospitality customers through fake hotel reservation pages impersonating Booking.com and other hotel services. The operation uses personalized reservation details including hotel names, dates, prices, guest information, and contact details to enhance credibility. Two main visual templates share the same underlying codebase: one closely mimics Booking.com while another uses generic Best Hotel Reservation branding. The kit employs advanced features including real-time card validation using Luhn checksums, interactive verification workflows, multi-language support spanning Japanese, Chinese, Korean, European languages and others, and three backend endpoints for tracking victim progression. Pages continue interaction after initial card submission through polling mechanisms that can present additional verification prompts. The campaign shows particular focus on Japanese hotels but is designed for global deployment across multiple countries and curr...","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-11-09T12:55:34.126000","created":"2026-11-09T12:44:59.049000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4507493218,"indicator":"homesdowttups.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-11-09T12:44:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4508643789,"indicator":"gardenstokyjp.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-11-09T12:44:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4516389654,"indicator":"reserv-advanced67746202.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-11-09T12:44:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4555385808,"indicator":"hotelchecckrsrv-krwo.world","type":"domain","created":"2026-11-09T12:44:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4572028120,"indicator":"advanced-reserv882689.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-11-09T12:44:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4572028121,"indicator":"confirmation-advanced-reserv203684.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-11-09T12:44:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4572028122,"indicator":"goldeshoms.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-11-09T12:44:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4572028123,"indicator":"guestnooks-homeset.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-11-09T12:44:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4572028124,"indicator":"gurades-homs.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-11-09T12:44:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4572028125,"indicator":"gustrwes-inforcheck.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-11-09T12:44:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4572028126,"indicator":"homeresbooks.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-11-09T12:44:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4572028127,"indicator":"staysuites-homebay.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-11-09T12:44:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4572028128,"indicator":"takayara-homs.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-11-09T12:44:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4572028129,"indicator":"tiamen-rooms.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-11-09T12:44:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4572028130,"indicator":"towntearse.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-11-09T12:44:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["personalized lures","booking.com impersonation","payment card theft","phishing","multi-language kit","3d secure","interactive verification","credential harvesting","hospitality"],"targeted_countries":["Japan"],"malware_families":[],"attack_ids":[],"references":["https:\/\/www.netcraft.com\/blog\/hospitality-phishing-cluster-uses-personalized-hotel-reservations-and-interactive-card-verification"],"industries":["Hospitality"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6aeeb5bc2f487ae6d84ea7e9","name":"ARTEX abuse expands as cybercriminals target financial sector","description":"In October 2026, the Cambodia-based threat actor Storm-3358 began leveraging the agentic AI offensive framework ARTEX to target financial organizations primarily in Southeast Asia and select global institutions. The group combines ARTEX with conventional automated tools to scan internet-connected systems, exploit vulnerabilities including anonymous file upload and server-side request forgery, and deploy open-source remote access trojans such as WISP, vshell, and AdaptixC2. ARTEX agents perform credential compromise, web shell deployment, lateral movement, privilege escalation, and data exfiltration at machine speed. This activity demonstrates an emerging trend of threat actors accelerating attack chains through agentic AI penetration testing frameworks, requiring defenders to similarly adopt AI-powered detection and response capabilities.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-11-09T12:54:09.199000","created":"2026-11-07T05:23:08.524000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"Storm-3358","indicators":[{"id":4333877662,"indicator":"91.92.240.238","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-11-07T05:23:09","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":"2026-12-07T05:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4555312234,"indicator":"178.16.54.129","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-11-07T05:23:09","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":"2026-12-07T05:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4558833208,"indicator":"31.77.229.35","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-11-07T05:23:09","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":"2026-12-07T05:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4568177220,"indicator":"85.11.168.45","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-11-07T05:23:09","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":"2026-12-07T05:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4568177221,"indicator":"178.15.54.129","type":"IPv4","created":"2026-11-07T05:23:09","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":"2026-12-07T05:00:00","is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["agentic ai","credential compromise","wisp","wisp rat","southeast asia","adaptixc2","artex","vshell","financial sector targeting"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":["ARTEX","WISP","vshell","AdaptixC2"],"attack_ids":["T1110.001","T1133","T1005","T1562","T1190","T1595.002","T1505.003","T1110.003","T1087","T1083","T1552.001","T1059.004","T1078","T1571","T1027","T1070.004","T1071.001","T1105","T1021.001"],"references":["https:\/\/www.microsoft.com\/en-us\/security\/blog\/2026\/11\/06\/artex-abuse-expands-as-cybercriminals-target-financial-sector\/"],"industries":["Finance"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6af1bfe0945ca03e48243de3","name":"Shai-Hulud Descendant Surfaces in Malicious Ruby Gem That Steals Credentials and Poisons AI Tools","description":"A malicious Ruby gem, strutil-core version 1.0.1, executes a 5.48 MB credential-stealing worm during installation. Published on November 1, 2026, by RubyGems account jamnajiea, the package was flagged 70 seconds after release and removed within five hours. The payload, a new build of the testmetest worm from the Miasma family descended from the Shai-Hulud toolkit, steals credentials from cloud services, CI systems, package registries, SSH, AI coding tools, and cryptocurrency wallets. It propagates through RubyGems, npm, PyPI, JFrog Artifactory, GitHub, GitLab, and SSH. The worm installs a Python backdoor controlled via signed GitHub commits, poisons AI tool configurations to maintain persistence, and includes a conditional wiper that deletes the user's home directory when a stolen GitHub token is revoked. The malware targets Linux and macOS systems on x86-64 and ARM64 architectures, excluding Russian-speaking locales.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-11-09T12:54:02.222000","created":"2026-11-09T12:43:12.759000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4546464026,"indicator":"aiarmor.website","type":"domain","created":"2026-11-09T12:43:13","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4567819920,"indicator":"paleasbest.top","type":"domain","created":"2026-11-09T12:43:13","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4567819921,"indicator":"https:\/\/paleasbest.top\/v1\/api","type":"URL","created":"2026-11-09T12:43:13","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4567819922,"indicator":"3b3f6e1bde0b28b015030a81a6d805b5b5306dc3f021e1102123971cfd83acc0","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-11-09T12:43:13","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4567819923,"indicator":"306c1deec402e8b4a6478e7f0fe02194bcd224d37d8fc6ba61ad1951e8abd7a9","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-11-09T12:43:13","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4567819924,"indicator":"c5264f3b9cf2f95c83a70b7dd7430aab8abc262b853dbbcd5386c3a8a9c74769","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-11-09T12:43:13","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4567819925,"indicator":"66c1c6b6b2c47e96fa5fd328338b939e1360511ab5eb2dda6d9112f592259d6b","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-11-09T12:43:13","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4567819926,"indicator":"c7ef186aa59b67d9b198a14f6dc8aaee6dd86510ac7c37d28f65d310cd846411","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-11-09T12:43:13","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4567819927,"indicator":"e29a5319888319b51345ab8e3e009938ee5c2b9ae5d6bdd053f4f44c98f309d3","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-11-09T12:43:13","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4567819928,"indicator":"c78daf27c42c3929758b24c2ef0baf65eea81b26b0fddfe8a5b748672d40d5f5","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-11-09T12:43:13","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4568250200,"indicator":"239ccc192a95f4668f2744d28d49569fa3efb8e3d6073cb461201fe36dd14860","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-11-09T12:43:13","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4568250201,"indicator":"http:\/\/paleasbest.top\/v1\/api","type":"URL","created":"2026-11-09T12:43:13","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4572028086,"indicator":"6d6aa7435c75628800f3af61e54aa6b3","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-11-09T12:43:13","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4572028087,"indicator":"4f7bfc300eeb76b5bb43e3331497a490a363445b","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-11-09T12:43:13","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["supply-chain","ruby-gem","ai-poisoning","miasma","shai-hulud","testmetest","wiper","credential-theft","strutil-core"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":["testmetest","Miasma","Shai-Hulud"],"attack_ids":[],"references":["https:\/\/socket.dev\/blog\/shai-hulud-descendant-malicious-ruby-gem"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6ac8a46214e2077a0bfe7409","name":"NEBULA: Seven Fake AI SDK Packages on npm Install a Windows RAT That Needs No DLL","description":"In late September 2026, an actor deployed seven malicious npm packages masquerading as a NebulaAI software development kit to deliver a Windows remote-access trojan. The operation, tracked as NEBULA, spans four sequential burner accounts (nebulallms through nebulallms4), with api-nebula and llm-nebula remaining downloadable. Each package presents a convincing AI client facade while hiding an obfuscated installation hook executing malicious logic. The underlying RAT operates exclusively through direct NT and win32k syscalls, bypassing standard DLL imports with an empty Import Address Table. Features include hidden-desktop remote control (HVNC), Kernel Streaming for camera and microphone monitoring, and Winlogon Shell persistence. The payload is a customized KNTRAT variant communicating with 65.87.7.132 using user-agent kntrat\/0xB15B00B6. The implant masquerades as conhost.exe and suppressed beaconing during analysis, consistent with embedded anti-analysis provisions.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-11-08T08:03:54.747000","created":"2026-10-09T08:22:58.387000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4517041457,"indicator":"api.nebulaai.dev","type":"hostname","created":"2026-10-09T08:22:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4518105344,"indicator":"5222dd57b8859e791a16abcf7f616bbc59f8cf248798c7c8c2ba800f0b52cd8c","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-10-09T08:22:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4518105345,"indicator":"8bc90df9b387849338d9c61a8d379cfbb0d70ea576c0e37e1fb07ba164921807","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-10-09T08:22:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4518105346,"indicator":"e99bab7b8bbbde7c821dae4ccfedfd1e608d65c466de9b08037c5ce5f56af3b1","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-10-09T08:22:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4518105347,"indicator":"f0d36ac2d75c81a4c3cbdbf2f717db858f2876e6a1cc74f2d36b729a1dd51a5e","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-10-09T08:22:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4518105348,"indicator":"https:\/\/api.nebulaai.dev\/v2","type":"URL","created":"2026-10-09T08:22:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4518105349,"indicator":"fact-register.md","type":"domain","created":"2026-10-09T08:22:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4518105350,"indicator":"uberip.com","type":"domain","created":"2026-10-09T08:22:59","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["npm","supply chain attack","hvnc","NEBULA"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":["KNTRAT"],"attack_ids":["T1056.001","T1036.005","T1543.003","T1082","T1106","T1055","T1125","T1090","T1547.001","T1027","T1573","T1195.002","T1012","T1564.003","T1059.003","T1134","T1027.002","T1071.001","T1569.002","T1056.004"],"references":["https:\/\/cdn.cloudsek.com\/cloudsek-blog-pdfs\/cloudsek-neb-qhe.pdf"],"industries":[],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6ac8a22f8d0ad1ea5f056ddc","name":"Unknown Threat Actor Uses AI-Driven ARTEX to Target South Korean Finance","description":"An unidentified threat actor, likely Chinese-speaking and financially motivated, conducted targeted attacks against South Korean financial institutions between late September and early October 2026, successfully exfiltrating data. The adversary utilized ARTEX, a Chinese-developed open-source agentic penetration testing tool, combined with large language models including DeepSeek v4.1-flash, GLM-5.3, and Grok 4.6. Analysis of exposed directories revealed Claude Code session histories, ARTEX configuration files, and operational details showing a two-server architecture involving Hong Kong-based infrastructure. The threat actor demonstrated sophisticated tradecraft by leveraging AI tooling to enhance operational tempo, enabling multiple intrusions within a compressed timeframe. Evidence suggests the attacker also researched Korean data breach marketplaces and Telegram channels for selling stolen information.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-11-08T08:03:54.747000","created":"2026-10-09T08:13:35.684000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4515940383,"indicator":"xcai.pro","type":"domain","created":"2026-10-09T08:13:36","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["llm-powered attacks","agentic ai","artex"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":["ARTEX"],"attack_ids":["T1592","T1133","T1530","T1071","T1190","T1567","T1589","T1595","T1090","T1059","T1583.003","T1041","T1078","T1203"],"references":["https:\/\/www.crowdstrike.com\/en-us\/blog\/unknown-threat-actor-uses-artex-to-target-south-korean-finance\/"],"industries":["Finance"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6ac84a1665712fe245b07ce7","name":"Threat Actors Exploit Critical AhsayCBS Flaws to Drop Webshells and XMRig Cryptominer","description":"Beginning October 7, 2026, threat actors exploited two critical vulnerabilities in AhsayCBS backup utility (CVE-2026-105133 and CVE-2026-105134) to achieve unauthenticated remote code execution on exposed systems. The attackers chained these vulnerabilities together, first bypassing authentication and then executing code with SYSTEM privileges. Post-exploitation activities included deploying JSP webshells, installing XMRig cryptocurrency miners disguised as Microsoft Edge processes, and dropping an AI-assisted PowerShell script that monitors and terminates Task Manager to hide mining operations. The attackers established persistence through a fake Windows service named MicrosoftEdgeUpdateSvc and utilized a vulnerable WinRing0x64.sys kernel driver to enable kernel-level hardware access for optimized mining performance. All AhsayCBS versions through 10.3.4 are affected, with managed service providers being the primary targets.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-11-08T01:03:47.635000","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:42.212000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"","indicators":[{"id":4205215990,"indicator":"xmr.kryptex.network","type":"hostname","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:43","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4512925779,"indicator":"CVE-2026-105133","type":"CVE","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:43","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4512925780,"indicator":"CVE-2026-105134","type":"CVE","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:43","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4517878183,"indicator":"4d0c11446fb8544b2336e4fc37cf232f","type":"FileHash-MD5","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:43","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4517878184,"indicator":"6cbdf36c511d664d5b0e119a23c2437d377d11a6","type":"FileHash-SHA1","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:43","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4517878185,"indicator":"05f69ae6b2b89c1c4dcf836bff032232f11bf0109f2b498e2345045d06139034","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:43","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4517878186,"indicator":"481728a7c9c4c02be07051d9c1958d902ea6397ebb8952ab83944818e3d25d21","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:43","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null},{"id":4517878187,"indicator":"4dcb0202fe8b2d4d7b183764e38184cd6ed50132786cc7e7d1f7f4bce1dd6f3d","type":"FileHash-SHA256","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:43","content":"","title":"","description":"","expiration":null,"is_active":1,"role":null}],"tags":["kernel driver exploitation","ahsaycbs","cryptomining","webshell","xmrig","msp targeting"],"targeted_countries":[],"malware_families":["XMRig"],"attack_ids":["T1036.005","T1564","T1543.003","T1608.001","T1190","T1505.003","T1036.004","T1057","T1059.001","T1571","T1059.003","T1071.001","T1105","T1569.002","T1124"],"references":["https:\/\/www.huntress.com\/blog\/ahsaycbs-flaws-exploit"],"industries":["Technology"],"extract_source":[],"more_indicators":false},{"id":"6ac84a166254b974f23968a2","name":"MATCHBOIL: New tricks, same old evil intentions","description":"ESET researchers documented the evolution of MATCHBOIL, a custom C# downloader used by Russia-aligned APT group UAC-0099. The malware downloads payloads from command-and-control servers, installs them, and establishes persistence on victim machines. Development traces back to April 2024, with continuous improvements through April 2026. Early versions used Unicode symbol obfuscation and custom string encryption, while later iterations employed the Eziriz .NET Reactor obfuscator. UAC-0099 progressively added sandbox detection methods, modified persistence mechanisms from registry keys to scheduled tasks, and introduced deceptive graphical interfaces. All observed victims were Ukrainian organizations across transportation, manufacturing, and energy sectors. The group typically distributes MATCHBOIL through spearphishing emails containing malicious links that download VBScript files. MATCHBOIL often delivers MATCHWOK backdoor as its final payload.","author_name":"AlienVault","modified":"2026-11-08T01:03:47.635000","created":"2026-10-09T01:57:42.729000","revision":2,"tlp":"white","public":1,"adversary":"UAC-009